    "localmaxxing": {
      "backend": null,
      "hardware_label": "RTX 3080",
      "notes": "Companion to the Q4_K_M entry on the same card, for the quant-vs-speed curve: Q6_K gives 278 tok/s in 8266 MiB versus Q4_K_M at 328 tok/s in 6546 MiB, both at 128K context and both fully resident. Sparse MoE, 8B total with ~1B active per token, which is why decode is far above a dense 8B. Measured on an RTX 3080 10GB. Decode is the MEDIAN of 3 reps, not the best. Prompt is deliberately non-repetitive (repeated filler inflates decode on speculative setups by ~25%) and ignore_eos is set so output token count is identical across runs. Peak VRAM 8266 MiB with 212 MiB host-shared; elevated host-shared only indicates spill when the decode rate drops with it.",
      "observed_command": "llama-server \\\n  -m LFM2.5-8B-A1B-Q6_K.gguf \\\n  --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8099 \\\n  --device CUDA0 --n-gpu-layers 99 \\\n  --ctx-size 128000 \\\n  --flash-attn on \\\n  --cache-type-k q8_0 --cache-type-v q8_0 \\\n  --parallel 1 --jinja \\\n  --spec-type none",
